          "Identifies and addresses edge cases; improves test coverage."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Sets engineering excellence standards adopted by others.",
          "Delivers complex systems with exceptional reliability and maintainability.",
          "Introduces patterns and practices that sustainably improve codebase quality."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Defect rates, on-call incidents tied to code changes",
        "Unit/integration test coverage and effectiveness",
        "Code review feedback frequency and severity",
        "Refactoring or tech debt reduction initiatives"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery and Ownership",
      "weight_percent": 20,
      "description": "Ability to scope, plan, and deliver work predictably while owning outcomes end-to-end.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Misses deadlines or requires frequent reprioritization from others.",
          "Hands off issues without ensuring resolution."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Meets timelines for simpler tasks but struggles with larger work.",
          "Needs support to unblock issues and coordinate dependencies."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Plans and delivers commitments reliably.",
          "Owns tasks from design to deployment and post-release follow-up."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Coordinates cross-team dependencies and de-risks delivery.",
          "Anticipates risks; adjusts plans and communicates proactively."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Leads delivery of complex, multi-team initiatives with predictable outcomes.",
          "Establishes repeatable execution processes adopted by others."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Roadmap commitments met vs. planned",
        "Jira/issue throughput and cycle time",
        "Risk logs and mitigation plans",
        "Postmortems demonstrating ownership"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "System Design and Architecture",
      "weight_percent": 15,
      "description": "Designing scalable, reliable, and cost-effective systems; making sound architectural decisions.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Designs tightly coupled solutions that limit extensibility.",
          "Neglects reliability, performance, or cost considerations."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Produces workable designs for small components with guidance.",
          "Inconsistently considers non-functional requirements."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Creates clear designs that balance trade-offs and scale appropriately.",
          "Documents architecture decisions and rationales."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Leads design of complex systems; drives design reviews effectively.",
          "Optimizes for cost, performance, and operability with data."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Defines architectural vision and standards across teams.",
          "Anticipates long-term evolution and avoids systemic pitfalls."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Design docs and ADRs",
        "Load/performance test results",
        "Architecture review feedback",
        "Cost projections and optimizations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Collaboration and Communication",
      "weight_percent": 10,
      "description": "Clarity, transparency, and effectiveness in working with teammates and stakeholders.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Communication is unclear or inconsistent; creates confusion.",
          "Resistant to feedback; difficult to collaborate with."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Shares updates but omits key details or timing.",
          "Accepts feedback but needs reminders to follow through."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Communicates clearly, timely, and adjusts style to audience.",
          "Engages in constructive feedback; contributes to healthy team dynamics."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Facilitates alignment across disciplines; resolves conflicts.",
          "Mentors others in communication best practices."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Trusted communicator for high-stakes topics; elevates org clarity.",
          "Builds frameworks for effective collaboration adopted by teams."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Status updates, RFC discussions",
        "Meeting facilitation notes",
        "Stakeholder satisfaction feedback",
        "Peer feedback on collaboration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Problem Solving and Debugging",
      "weight_percent": 10,
      "description": "Diagnosing issues, using data to identify root causes, and implementing robust fixes.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Struggles to isolate problems; applies trial-and-error fixes.",
          "Introduces regressions while addressing defects."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Solves straightforward bugs with guidance; limited use of data.",
          "Fixes address symptoms more than root causes."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Uses systematic debugging and observability data to find root causes.",
          "Implements fixes with tests and preventive measures."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Resolves complex, elusive issues quickly; improves tooling/observability.",
          "Guides others in effective debugging techniques."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Preempts classes of failures through systemic improvements.",
          "Establishes incident response and debugging best practices."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Incident timelines and resolution quality",
        "Bug recurrence rates",
        "Observability dashboards and alerts added",
        "Runbooks and troubleshooting guides"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Security, Reliability, and Compliance",
      "weight_percent": 5,
      "description": "Practices that ensure secure, reliable, compliant systems and processes.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Overlooks security basics; creates reliability risks.",
          "Ignores compliance or privacy requirements."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Follows checklists with supervision; gaps remain under pressure.",
          "Limited threat modeling or resilience thinking."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Implements secure defaults and reliability patterns.",
          "Documents and follows compliance requirements."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Leads threat modeling and resilience reviews.",
          "Drives improvements in SLAs/SLOs and compliance processes."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Shapes org-wide security and reliability standards.",
          "Quantifiably reduces risk and compliance burden."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Security review outcomes",
        "SLA/SLO adherence",
        "Audit findings and remediation",
        "Secrets management practices"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Mentorship and Knowledge Sharing",
      "weight_percent": 5,
      "description": "Uplifting others through coaching, documentation, and learning culture.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Rarely shares knowledge; creates silos.",
          "Feedback is unconstructive or absent."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Answers direct questions; limited proactive mentoring.",
          "Provides occasional code review tips."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Mentors peers/juniors; provides actionable feedback.",
          "Contributes to docs, runbooks, and internal talks."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Develops onboarding materials and learning paths.",
          "Coaches multiple engineers; measurable skill growth."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Builds a scalable mentorship program; fosters learning culture.",
          "Recognized as a go-to educator across teams."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Mentorship logs and mentee feedback",
        "Documentation contributions",
        "Workshops or tech talks",
        "Code review quality and participation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Product and Customer Impact",
      "weight_percent": 5,
      "description": "Understanding user needs and delivering business/customer value.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Builds features without understanding user impact.",
          "Limited consideration of usability or business goals."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Implements requirements literally; misses edge user cases.",
          "Needs guidance translating goals into technical scope."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Connects work to user outcomes; makes pragmatic trade-offs.",
          "Proposes small improvements informed by data or feedback."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Drives product improvements through insights and experiments.",
          "Balances short/long-term value; measurable customer impact."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Shapes product strategy with data and technical perspective.",
          "Consistently delivers features that materially move key metrics."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Feature adoption and usage metrics",
        "A/B test outcomes",
        "Customer/PM feedback",
        "Usability improvements and defect reduction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Operational Excellence",
      "weight_percent": 5,
      "description": "On-call effectiveness, observability, deployment safety, and run-time efficiency.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Creates operational toil; poor runbooks and alert hygiene.",
          "Unreliable on-call participation."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Responds to incidents with guidance; slow root cause identification.",
          "Basic dashboards and alerts exist but are noisy."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Maintains healthy on-call; clear runbooks and actionable alerts.",
          "Deployments are safe with rollbacks and monitoring."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Reduces toil via automation; improves latency and costs.",
          "Leads postmortems and systemic fixes."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Defines SRE-aligned practices; eliminates classes of incidents.",
          "Sets high reliability standards adopted org-wide."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "MTTR/MTBF trends",
        "Change failure rate and deployment frequency",
        "Runbook quality and alert signal-to-noise",
        "Cost/latency improvements"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Initiative and Leadership",
      "weight_percent": 10,
      "description": "Proactivity, influence without authority, and ability to drive change.",
      "behaviors_by_level": {
        "1": [
          "Waits for direction; avoids responsibility for outcomes.",
          "Resistant to change and feedback."
        ],
        "2": [
          "Takes initiative on assigned tasks; limited scope influence.",
          "Participates in change but needs guidance."
        ],
        "3": [
          "Identifies improvements and executes with minimal guidance.",
          "Influences peers through data and empathy."
        ],
        "4": [
          "Leads cross-team initiatives; earns trust across functions.",
          "Navigates ambiguity; aligns stakeholders to outcomes."
        ],
        "5": [
          "Drives strategic initiatives that reshape team/org trajectory.",
          "Builds coalitions and creates long-lasting mechanisms."
        ]
      },
      "evidence_examples": [
        "Initiatives proposed and completed",
        "Cross-team alignment artifacts",
        "Stakeholder testimonials",
        "Measured impact of change initiatives"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "overall_rating_guidance": {
    "method": "Weighted average of competency ratings, calibrated by level expectations and scope of impact.",
    "calibration_notes": [
      "Consider scope and complexity relative to role level (e.g., IC2 vs IC5).",
      "Sustained performance weighs more than isolated highs/lows.",
      "Account for systemic constraints outside the engineer’s control."
    ]
  },
  "role_adjustments": [
    {
      "role": "Junior/Entry (IC1-IC2)",
      "adjustments": "Increase weight on Technical Execution and Collaboration; reduce System Design and Leadership expectations."
    },
    {
      "role": "Mid-level (IC3)",
      "adjustments": "Use default weights; emphasize reliable delivery and growing design ownership."
    },
    {
      "role": "Senior (IC4)",
      "adjustments": "Increase weight on System Design, Operational Excellence, and Mentorship."
    },
    {
      "role": "Staff+ (IC5+)",
      "adjustments": "Increase weight on Architecture, Leadership, and Org Impact; evaluate multi-team influence."
    }
  ],
  "review_process": [
    "Self-assessment against each competency with examples.",
    "Peer and cross-functional feedback collection.",
    "Manager assessment using rubric and evidence.",
    "Calibration across teams to ensure consistency.",
    "Finalize ratings, document growth areas and next-step goals."
  ],
  "development_plan_template": {
    "strengths": "List top 2-3 strengths with concrete examples.",
    "growth_areas": "List 2-3 areas with specific skill gaps and desired outcomes.",
    "goals_smart": [
      "Specific: Clear behavior or skill to acquire.",
      "Measurable: Define success metrics.",
      "Achievable: Realistic given time/resources.",
      "Relevant: Tied to role/level expectations.",
      "Time-bound: Target dates and milestones."
    ],
    "actions": [
      "Training/courses and reading",
      "Mentorship or pairing plans",
      "Shadowing/rotation opportunities",
      "Project assignments to practice skills"
    ],
    "checkpoints": "Monthly check-ins to track progress and adjust plan."
  },
  "anti_bias_guidance": [
    "Focus on documented outcomes and observed behaviors, not personality or intent.",
    "Use consistent evidence types across reports.",
    "Account for unequal opportunities, on-call load, and project risk.",
    "Avoid recency bias; consider the full review period.",
    "Cross-check language for gendered or culturally biased terms."
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "created_by": "HR/Engineering",
    "last_updated": "2025-10-02",
    "notes": "This rubric is a guideline; use judgment with evidence and calibrations."
  }
}
